  "reasons": {
    "src/core/architecture-reference.js || src/pages/architecture-framework.data.js": "DELIBERATE two-surface split - 1023 windows (was 1015 at batch #23 phase 1, 890 at batch #22, 839 at batch #19), the largest in the repo. architecture-reference.js is the AI-readable module, architecture-framework.data.js is the human page, and the overlap IS the mechanism; the two deliberately differ in LENGTH (the page paraphrases). The risk is DIVERGENCE, not copying. Do NOT delete either side on the strength of this number. Growth from a handoff batch is EXPECTED here: batch #22 (22 handoffs) added +51 windows and batch #23 (30 handoffs) added +125, precisely because both surfaces must carry the same slice - banked deliberately, not silently. MEASURED 2026-09-23 (batch #23): the two AGREE on CONTRACT_REGISTER_LAST_UPDATED (identical string, both batch #23), both gained the same 28 slice bullets and 16 route contracts, and the splice was verified against a pre-splice backup so each array's delta is exact (+28/+28 bullets, +16/+16 routes) rather than asserted. reference.js additionally carries a historical batch #6 marker the page lacks - an asymmetry, not a live contradiction. What is still UNGUARDED is the agreement itself: nothing fails the build if one surface is updated and the other is not. They diverged once already (batch #17 stamped a date in one and not the other) and only a human reading both found it.",
    "src/components/SignalCard.jsx || src/pages/SignalsOverviewPage.jsx": "DELIBERATE A/B variant, and the page says so in code: 'Card A stays here, reachable at ?variant=A - removing a live variant is a decision, not a refactor.' Card B is the shared component; Card A is the legacy design used for side-by-side comparison. The two button labels HAVE diverged (SignalCard 'Buy (Long)' vs OpportunityCard 'Buy CFD') - that is the experiment, not a bug. Deleting OpportunityCard would remove a live variant.",
    "nest/src/modules/directives/implementations/macd-divergence.directive.ts || nest/src/modules/directives/implementations/obv-divergence.directive.ts": "DONE 2026-09-21 - was 34 windows of DUPLICATED SCORING ALGORITHM, now 4. The five swing/divergence helpers moved to nest/src/modules/directives/utils/divergence.ts and all three directives import them. What REMAINS here is imports and the IDirective class preamble - structure, not logic. Proven behaviour-preserving: 108 golden cases (12 seeds x 3 bar-counts x 3 directives, 29 of them exercising the strength formula) produced a BYTE-IDENTICAL result before and after (sha256 333719E6...). The three strength CALIBRATIONS deliberately stay per-directive and now sit side by side in one place; see StrengthModel in utils/divergence.ts for why they differ.",
    "src/pages/ProtocolTrailPage.jsx || src/pages/SinglesMonitorPage.jsx": "NOT deliberate - extraction candidate, measured 2026-09-19. Both consume the same breakdown payload and repeat its mapping (breakouts / subScores / subMaxTotals) across six separate blocks. Not done.",
    "nest/src/modules/system/architecture-manifest.controller.ts || src/core/architecture-reference.js": "NOT deliberate - the controller EMBEDS the pipeline-step descriptions that architecture-reference.js also declares, so the same prose exists in the backend and the frontend. Single-source candidate. Not done.",
